# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Line-ending policy
#  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Backend (Windows) and vault (Obsidian / CloudStation, LF-native)
#  share proposal + handoff + decision files via proposal_sync.
#  If git keeps converting LF → CRLF on checkout, every commit
#  re-introduces drift the sync health-check flags as conflicts
#  (the bug observed on 2026-05-24 that blocked the kanban watcher).
#
#  Fix: force LF for all text that crosses the backend/vault boundary.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# All text files: normalize to LF on commit, do NOT convert back to CRLF
# on checkout. This means new clones on Windows ALSO get LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Markdown — proposals, handoffs, decisions, runbooks: explicitly LF
# (these are the ones that cross the backend/vault boundary)
*.md text eol=lf
*.markdown text eol=lf

# YAML configs — read by both Python and ruamel.yaml on both ends
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# JSON — golden fixtures, schemas
*.json text eol=lf

# Python sources
*.py text eol=lf

# Shell + batch — Windows batch needs CRLF, *nix shell needs LF
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files — git should never touch
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gguf binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db binary
